# home/

Working example feature for ${PROJECT_NAME}. Compose screen that reads a
hardcoded `Status.OK` from `HomeRepositoryImpl`.

> **Intentionally tiny.** This feature exists to demonstrate the strict
> 4-subfolder rule, not to demo auth, DB access, or live network calls. Do
> NOT expand it. If you need a network or auth example, copy
> `_feature_template/` and build a separate feature.

## The strict 4-subfolder rule

| Subfolder | What lives here | File suffix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [`ui/`](ui/) | Compose screen (`HomeScreen.kt`) + screen-local composables | `*Screen.kt` |
| [`viewmodel/`](viewmodel/) | `HomeViewModel.kt` + `HomeUiState` data class | `*ViewModel.kt` |
| [`domain/`](domain/) | `HomeRepository` interface + `GetHomeStatusUseCase` | `*Repository.kt`, `*UseCase.kt` |
| [`data/`](data/) | `HomeRepositoryImpl` (hardcoded `Status.OK`) | `*RepositoryImpl.kt` |

## How it wires together

1. `MainApplication.onCreate()` constructs `AppGraph(this)`.
2. `AppGraph` builds `HomeRepositoryImpl` and exposes it via `homeRepository`.
3. `HomeScreen` reads `MainApplication.graph.homeRepository` and feeds it
   into `HomeViewModel.factory(...)`.
4. The VM emits `HomeUiState(isLoading=false, status=OK)`.

No Hilt, no Room, no KSP — see `app/build.gradle.kts` for the rationale.

